From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Subject: [PATCH] controller: preserve negotiated peer profile

AP-Autoconfiguration Search establishes the agent's EasyMesh profile. A
profile-less Topology Response can subsequently arrive from the colocated
ieee1905 responder during warm reconstruction. Treating that response as a
fresh Profile-1 negotiation downgrades the AL node and every radio, after
which valid Profile-3 WSC M1 retries fail validation and the BSS inventory
cannot be reconstructed.

The controller also has one global AL-node object but multiple agent peers.
Using that global object's last profile to validate a radio-specific message
makes concurrent agents overwrite one another. Resolve the peer profile from
the radio's data model first and retain the AL node only as a final legacy
fallback.

An absent Profile TLV is not evidence of a downgrade. Preserve the profile
already recorded in the device model, AL node, or local transaction; use
Profile 1 only when no negotiated value exists.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 51 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2324,21 +2324,43 @@ em_profile_type_t em_configuration_t::get_peer_profile_from_al_em()
 
 em_profile_type_t em_configuration_t::get_peer_profile_from_al_em()
 {
-    // Use the locally cached profile as a safe fallback for validation.
-    em_profile_type_t fallback = (m_peer_profile == em_profile_type_reserved) ? em_profile_type_1 : m_peer_profile;
+    auto valid_profile = [](em_profile_type_t profile) {
+        return profile > em_profile_type_reserved && profile < em_profile_type_max;
+    };
+
+    // The controller owns one AL-node EM but communicates with multiple
+    // agents.  Therefore that global AL node cannot be the source of truth
+    // for a particular radio's peer.  Prefer the peer-specific data model
+    // and radio profile established during discovery/onboarding.
+    dm_easy_mesh_t *dm = get_data_model();
+    if (dm != nullptr) {
+        em_profile_type_t dm_profile = dm->get_device_info()->profile;
+        if (valid_profile(dm_profile)) {
+            return dm_profile;
+        }
+    }
+
+    em_profile_type_t radio_profile = get_profile_type();
+    if (valid_profile(radio_profile)) {
+        return radio_profile;
+    }
+
+    if (valid_profile(m_peer_profile)) {
+        return m_peer_profile;
+    }
 
     em_mgr_t *mgr = get_mgr();
     if (mgr == nullptr) {
-        return fallback;
+        return em_profile_type_1;
     }
 
     em_t *al_em = mgr->get_al_node();
     if (al_em == nullptr) {
-        return fallback;
+        return em_profile_type_1;
     }
 
     em_profile_type_t al_profile = al_em->get_peer_profile();
-    return (al_profile == em_profile_type_reserved) ? fallback : al_profile;
+    return valid_profile(al_profile) ? al_profile : em_profile_type_1;
 }
 
 bool em_configuration_t::remove_non_mlo_sta_assoc(dm_easy_mesh_t *dm,
@@ -2844,10 +2866,25 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
         m_peer_profile = profile;
         em_printfout("Topology response received from %s with profile: %d", util::mac_to_string(src_al_mac).c_str(), m_peer_profile);
     } else {
-        // MultiAP profile TLV is mandatory for profile >= em_profile_type_2.
-        // FALL back to profile 1 for backward compatibility with earlier EasyMesh specifications.
-        m_peer_profile = em_profile_type_1;
-        em_printfout("Topology response received from %s with no profile TLV, assuming profile: %d", util::mac_to_string(src_al_mac).c_str(), m_peer_profile);
+        // A profile-less response is valid for a legacy Profile-1 peer, but it
+        // is not evidence that an already negotiated Profile-2/3 peer has
+        // downgraded.  In particular, the colocated ieee1905 responder can
+        // race the EasyMesh response during warm reconstruction.  Preserve
+        // the profile recorded by AP-Autoconfiguration Search (and persisted
+        // in the device model) instead of poisoning every radio's WSC
+        // validation state with Profile 1.
+        em_profile_type_t preserved_profile = dm->m_device.m_device_info.profile;
+        if (preserved_profile == em_profile_type_reserved && al_em != nullptr) {
+            preserved_profile = al_em->get_peer_profile();
+        }
+        if (preserved_profile == em_profile_type_reserved) {
+            preserved_profile = m_peer_profile;
+        }
+        if (preserved_profile == em_profile_type_reserved) {
+            preserved_profile = em_profile_type_1;
+        }
+        m_peer_profile = preserved_profile;
+        em_printfout("Topology response received from %s with no profile TLV, preserving profile: %d", util::mac_to_string(src_al_mac).c_str(), m_peer_profile);
     }
     // Update the peer profile in the AL node
     if (al_em != nullptr) {
